  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Variables: Anatomy & Purpose",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Input variables are a module's function parameters. They parameterize a config without editing its source."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "variable \"region\" {",
            "  type        = string        # shape gate",
            "  default     = \"us-east-1\"   # optional now",
            "  description = \"Deploy region\"",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Seven Meta-Args",
          "items": [
            "`type`, `default`, `description`",
            "`validation`, `sensitive`",
            "`nullable`, `ephemeral` (1.10+)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reference Rules",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reference as `var.name` — never `variable.name`",
            "`\"${var.name}\"` is legacy; write bare `var.name`",
            "Names must be unique per module",
            "Root vars come from CLI and environment",
            "Child vars come from `module` block arguments"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Reserved Names",
          "items": [
            "`count`, `for_each`, `source`, `version`",
            "`providers`, `depends_on`",
            "`lifecycle`, `locals`"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Required vs Optional",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Written",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "no `default`",
              "required; prompts at plan"
            ],
            [
              "`default = x`",
              "optional, falls back to x"
            ],
            [
              "`nullable = false`",
              "explicit `null` rejected"
            ],
            [
              "`nullable = true`",
              "the default; `null` allowed"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Passing `null` where a default exists uses the default",
            "A common source of surprise in wrapper modules",
            "The prompt text is the `description` field",
            "`terraform-docs` harvests descriptions into README"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Evaluation Order",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "tfvars / CLI",
              "`var.x` resolved",
              "locals",
              "resources"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Variables resolve before any resource exists",
            "They cannot reference resources, data or other variables",
            "Unused declared variables are legal, just noise",
            "An undeclared value passed to a module is a hard error"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Variables: Anatomy & Purpose (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "module \"vpc\" {",
            "  source = \"./vpc\"",
            "  cidr   = var.cidr   # name must match",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "ephemeral = true (1.10+)",
          "text": "Usable during the operation but never written to state or plan files."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Primitives",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`string`, `number`, `bool` — that is the whole list",
            "One numeric type: no int/float split",
            "`number` covers 42 and 3.14 alike"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Collection vs Structural",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Collection",
                "lines": [
                  "`list(T)` ordered",
                  "`set(T)` unordered, deduped",
                  "`map(T)` string keys",
                  "Many values, ONE type"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Structural",
                "lines": [
                  "`object({...})` fixed keys",
                  "`tuple([...])` fixed positions",
                  "Many values, DIFFERENT types"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "type = object({",
            "  name = string",
            "  port = number   # each key its own type",
            "})",
            "type = tuple([string, number, bool])"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "optional() Keys",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "type = object({",
            "  proto = optional(string, \"http\")",
            "  tls   = optional(string)  # null if absent",
            "})"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`optional(k)` may be omitted; becomes `null`",
            "`optional(k, d)` supplies the default for you",
            "Beats a downstream `coalesce` at every use site",
            "Valid only on object attributes, nowhere else"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Automatic Conversion",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Value",
            "Target",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`\"5\"`",
              "`number`",
              "`5`"
            ],
            [
              "`true`",
              "`string`",
              "`\"true\"`"
            ],
            [
              "`[\"a\",\"a\",\"b\"]`",
              "`set(string)`",
              "2 elements"
            ],
            [
              "`{1 = \"x\"}`",
              "`map(string)`",
              "key coerced"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Type System",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Conversion happens only where unambiguous",
            "List to set dedupes and loses order for good",
            "Mismatch fails with `Invalid value for input variable`",
            "Caught at plan, before any provider API call"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The any Escape",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`any` infers a concrete type at call time",
            "It is not a wildcard that skips checking",
            "Omitting `type` entirely means `any`",
            "`any` defers every error to the usage site"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "type    = map(string)  # values all strings",
            "default = {",
            "  engine  = \"postgres\"",
            "  version = \"15\"       # quoted, not 15",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Strict vs any",
          "text": "Strict `object(...)` gives early errors and self-documenting modules; `any` gives flexibility and terrible error messages."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The validation Block",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "validation {",
            "  condition     = length(var.name) <= 32",
            "  error_message = \"Name is too long.\"",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Boolean `condition`; `error_message` shows when false",
            "Inside `condition` only `var.this_one` is visible",
            "No other variables, resources or data sources",
            "Several `validation` blocks per variable are allowed",
            "All run; every failure is reported at once"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "can and try",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "condition = can(",
            "  regex(\"^ami-[0-9a-f]{8,}$\", var.ami_id)",
            ")"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`can(expr)` swallows the error and returns a bool",
            "Idiomatic test for convertibility or shape",
            "`try(a, b, c)` returns the first that evaluates",
            "Use `try` for shape-tolerant lookups"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Condition Patterns",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Check",
            "Condition"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Membership",
              "`contains([\"dev\",\"prod\"], var.env)`"
            ],
            [
              "Range",
              "`var.port > 0 && var.port < 65536`"
            ],
            [
              "Length",
              "`length(var.name) <= 32`"
            ],
            [
              "Every element",
              "`alltrue([for s in var.cidrs : can(cidrnetmask(s))])`"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Validation Blocks & Custom Rules",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`error_message` must be a full sentence with a period",
            "Older versions enforced that strictly",
            "Validation runs at plan time, before providers",
            "Failing costs nothing: no API call, no state write"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Beyond One Variable",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "`validation`",
              "`precondition`",
              "apply",
              "`postcondition`",
              "`check` warns"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`precondition` / `postcondition` sit in a `lifecycle` block",
            "They CAN reference other resources and data",
            "`check` blocks (1.5+) warn without failing the apply"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Variable rejected but nothing hit AWS?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Validation runs during the plan graph walk",
            "Providers are not configured at that point",
            "So a typo fails in seconds, and for free"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Where policy lives",
          "text": "Validation catches typos early but pushes policy into modules; OPA or Sentinel keeps policy central and versioned once."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Six Sources, Ranked",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "spec": {
            "rows": [
              [
                "defaults",
                "`TF_VAR_*`"
              ],
              [
                "`terraform.tfvars`",
                "`.tfvars.json`"
              ],
              [
                "`*.auto.tfvars`",
                "`-var-file` / `-var`"
              ]
            ],
            "caption": "lowest to highest"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Later source wins for the same variable name",
            "Highest of all: the last `-var` on the command line",
            "`-var-file` and `-var` rank in command-line order",
            "`*.auto.tfvars` load alphabetically, so `02-override` beats `01-base`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Assigning Values & Precedence",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Auto-Loaded vs Explicit",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "File",
            "Loaded"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`terraform.tfvars`",
              "automatic"
            ],
            [
              "`terraform.tfvars.json`",
              "automatic"
            ],
            [
              "`prod.auto.tfvars`",
              "automatic"
            ],
            [
              "`prod.tfvars`",
              "only with `-var-file`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Environment Form",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "TF_VAR_region=us-west-2 terraform plan",
            "TF_VAR_tags='{team=\"core\"}'  # HCL in a string",
            "terraform plan -var 'list=[\"a\",\"b\"]'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Name is case-sensitive after the `TF_VAR_` prefix",
            "Complex values need HCL syntax inside the string",
            "`-var` quoting differs between bash and PowerShell",
            "HCP workspace variables sit at the `-var` level"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What tfvars Is Not",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Plain `name = value` assignments only",
            "No `variable` keyword, no functions, no resources",
            "No interpolation of other variables",
            "Definitions files apply to the ROOT module only",
            "Child modules get values via their `module` block"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Repo Hygiene",
          "items": [
            "Commit `terraform.tfvars.example`",
            "Gitignore `*.tfvars` holding secrets",
            "Never a real password in either"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "CI Behaviour",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Missing value fails: `No value for required variable`",
            "Pass `-input=false` so it errors instead of hanging"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Debug the ladder",
          "text": "Run `terraform console` under the same flags and evaluate `var.name` to see which source actually won."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What sensitive Does",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "variable \"db_password\" {",
            "  type      = string",
            "  sensitive = true   # hides from plan output",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Plan and apply print `(sensitive value)` instead",
            "Sensitivity is contagious: derived values inherit it",
            "State still holds the value in PLAINTEXT",
            "Redaction is a display feature, not encryption"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Sensitive Values & Secret Hygiene",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Propagation Rules",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An output built from it must declare `sensitive = true`",
            "`nonsensitive(expr)` strips the marking — auditable, never routine",
            "Forbidden in `count`, `for_each` and resource identifiers",
            "Provider schema-marked arguments redact on their own"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "sensitive vs ephemeral",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "sensitive = true",
                "lines": [
                  "Hidden in CLI output",
                  "Still written to state",
                  "Still in the plan file"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "ephemeral = true (1.10+)",
                "lines": [
                  "Never in state",
                  "Never in a plan file",
                  "Write-only args (1.11+) too"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Leak path",
            "What escapes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`terraform output -json`",
              "values UNREDACTED"
            ],
            [
              "`TF_LOG=trace`",
              "secret request bodies"
            ],
            [
              "state file",
              "everything, plaintext"
            ],
            [
              "CI job log",
              "both of the above"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Real Secret Sources",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Vault provider or a cloud secret manager",
            "CI-injected `TF_VAR_*` at run time",
            "Not tfvars files committed to the repo"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why can a sensitive value not drive `for_each`?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Keys become resource addresses in plan and state",
            "Every log line would then print the secret",
            "Terraform blocks it: `Invalid for_each argument`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "After A Leak",
          "items": [
            "Rotate at the source, not in tfvars",
            "Deleting the file changes nothing",
            "Never attach trace logs to public issues"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "State is the boundary",
          "text": "Encrypt state at rest, lock it, and restrict access: S3 plus SSE plus strict IAM is the baseline."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Declaring Locals",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "locals {",
            "  prefix = \"${var.project}-${var.env}\"",
            "}",
            "# used later as local.prefix (singular)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Named intermediate values: a module's private constants",
            "Block is `locals`, the reference is `local.name`",
            "Several `locals` blocks merge into one namespace",
            "Cannot be set from outside; not part of the interface"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Locals: Named Expressions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Each May Touch",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "A variable sees",
                "lines": [
                  "Its own literal default",
                  "Nothing else at all"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "A local sees",
                "lines": [
                  "`var.*` and other locals",
                  "Resources and data sources",
                  "Any function or expression"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Locals are lazily evaluated and form a DAG",
            "A circular reference is a plan-time error",
            "No runtime cost: resolved during graph evaluation",
            "Not stored in state on their own"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Classic Uses",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "tags = merge(var.tags, {",
            "  ManagedBy = \"terraform\"",
            "})",
            "size = var.env == \"prod\" ? \"m5.large\" : \"t3.micro\"",
            "nets = { for i, c in var.cidrs : \"net-${i}\" => c }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`local.prefix` carries the naming convention",
            "`local.tags` merges caller tags with your own",
            "`local.nets` builds a map ready for `for_each`",
            "Resource blocks stay short and readable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Limits",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No `type`, no `description`, no `validation`",
            "Type is inferred; documentation lives in comments",
            "Overusing locals hides logic behind indirection",
            "A local read once is often worth inlining"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Not The Interface",
          "items": [
            "Callers cannot set a local",
            "Callers cannot read a local",
            "Publish an output if they need it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Variable for what callers choose; local for what you compute from those choices."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Declaring an Output",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "output \"vpc_id\" {",
            "  value       = aws_vpc.main.id",
            "  description = \"ID of the VPC\"",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Root outputs print after apply",
            "Read them with `terraform output` or `-json`",
            "`terraform output -raw name` gives an unquoted string",
            "Child outputs are read as `module.vpc.vpc_id`",
            "That is the ONLY way a parent sees inside a module"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Outputs: The Return Values",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Argument",
            "Role"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`value`",
              "the published expression"
            ],
            [
              "`description`",
              "documents the contract"
            ],
            [
              "`sensitive`",
              "redacts from CLI output"
            ],
            [
              "`depends_on`",
              "ordering the expression hides"
            ],
            [
              "`precondition`",
              "asserts before publishing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "State and Cross-Stack",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "data \"terraform_remote_state\" \"net\" {",
            "  backend = \"s3\"",
            "  config  = { bucket = \"tf-state\" }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Outputs are persisted in state — that is how this works",
            "Read `data.terraform_remote_state.net.outputs.vpc_id`",
            "Removing an output breaks every consumer of it",
            "`ephemeral = true` outputs are never persisted"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Timing",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Outputs are evaluated after apply",
            "Unknown at plan prints `(known after apply)`",
            "A `precondition` guarantees the value before publishing",
            "`depends_on` forces order the expression cannot show"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shape The Contract",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefer narrow explicit outputs over whole resource objects",
            "Whole objects leak fields and churn the diff",
            "An output cannot be referenced inside its own module",
            "Compute a `local` and output that local instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "resource",
              "`output`",
              "state file",
              "`remote_state`",
              "other stack"
            ]
          }
        },
